 (407, 'Let us write – I (Descriptive essay sample)', [
  'A MONSOON MORNING AT PULICAT LAKE | Last July my family visited Pulicat Lake, about an hour from our village in SPSR Nellore district. It was a cool, cloudy morning.',
  'The grey sky met the silver water at the horizon. Thousands of pink flamingos stood on thin legs, while pelicans glided above. The cool breeze carried the smell of salt and wet sand, and fishermen sang as they pulled their nets.',
  'Suddenly, the clouds opened and soft rain began to fall. The flamingos rose together like a pink cloud. I stood still, feeling tiny drops on my face and joy in my heart.',
  'That morning taught me that nature is the greatest artist. We must protect lakes like Pulicat so that our birds and fishermen can live happily.']),
 (408, 'Let us write – II (Conversation on Uppada coast)', [
  'Me: Did you read the news about Uppada coast in Kakinada district?',
  'Friend: Yes! The sea has swallowed more than 1,360 acres of land in eight villages.',
  'Me: Hundreds of houses, two guest houses and ancient temples have disappeared. It is really sad.',
  'Friend: Fishermen lose their homes and livelihood every year. Only 84 acres were lost till 1956, but now it is over 1,360!',
  'Me: Unlike Chandipur, where the sea goes and comes back, here the sea keeps eating the land. The government must build strong sea walls and groynes.',
  'Friend: We should also grow mangroves and casuarina trees along the coast, like the Sundarbans, to reduce erosion.',
  'Me: Yes, and families should be moved to safe places. Let us write a letter to the Collector about it.']),
